WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.090
One or two degrees of warming sounds
far too small to matter to wildlife.

2
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:09.440
On a mountain in New Guinea,
the birds were surveyed in 1965,

3
00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.590
and again in 2012.

4
00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:15.420
For most species, both limits of
their range had moved upslope,

5
00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:18.730
by about 100 m on average.

6
00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.340
So why can such a small
warming force species to move,

7
00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:24.420
or vanish from a place?

8
00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:27.500
In this mission, you'll map
where a species can live,

9
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.170
on a mountain and across a continent.

10
00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:35.610
Then you'll test real survey data, and
judge what it can and cannot tell you.

11
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:40.070
Your mission: explain how such a
small warming can move species,

12
00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:41.800
or wipe them out of a place.
